      "content": "You are absolutely right to be concerned about logical flaws in tests, as they can create blind spots that destructive bugs exploit before production. To mitigate this, you should implement multiple independent test families and regularly rotate or update test scenarios to prevent them from becoming routine blind spots. Additionally, consider using external, third-party tools for safety and isolation to reduce the risk of a single logic flaw becoming a systemic vulnerability.",
